Package: nexus-control-center
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nexus-ui (= ${binary:Version}),
 libkscreen-bin, xkb-data, polkitd, pkexec, pulseaudio-utils, python3, passwd,
 accountsservice, nexus-hardening, apt, locales, tzdata, util-linux, libkf6config-bin,
 qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs, qml6-module-qtquick-effects
Recommends: network-manager, bluez, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, upower, power-profiles-daemon,
 udisks2, smartmontools, nexus-updater, nexus-security-center
Suggests: network-manager-openvpn
Description: NEXUS Control Center
 The system settings application of NEXUS OS: network (Wi-Fi, wired and
 proxy, Bluetooth, VPN), hardware (displays, sound, power, keyboard, mouse
 and touchpad, storage), personalisation (appearance, accessibility,
 startup applications), privacy and security (users, privacy, firewall,
 security overview) and system (updates, region and language, date and
 time, about), each talking to the real system service.

Package: nexus-network-center
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nexus-ui (= ${binary:Version}),
 network-manager, iproute2, iputils-ping, python3, pkexec, polkitd
Recommends: traceroute, bind9-dnsutils, tcpdump
Suggests: wireshark, network-manager-openvpn
Description: NEXUS Network Center
 Network interfaces, addresses, routes, DNS, sockets and connections, Wi-Fi
 and VPN management through NetworkManager, diagnostics (ping, traceroute,
 DNS lookup, port check) and packet capture through a narrowly scoped
 privileged helper. Packet capture is for networks you are authorised to
 monitor.

Package: nexus-arsenal
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nexus-ui (= ${binary:Version}),
 nexus-arsenal-data (= ${source:Version}), dpkg, apt
Recommends: packagekit, polkitd, nexus-terminal
Description: NEXUS Arsenal - security tool profile manager
 Browse the NEXUS Arsenal profiles (web, network, red team, blue team,
 forensics, reverse engineering, development), see which tools are installed
 and install or remove a whole profile or single tools through PackageKit.
 Tools that are not available from the NEXUS repositories are listed with a
 link to their official source; nothing is downloaded behind your back.
 .
 The manager installs no tools by itself.
 .
 These tools are for authorised security testing, research, defence and
 education only: use them on systems you own or have explicit written
 permission to test, and follow the law that applies to you. They come with no
 warranty.

Package: nexus-arsenal-data
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: NEXUS Arsenal - profile manifests
 Machine-readable descriptions of the NEXUS Arsenal security tool profiles:
 which Debian packages belong to a profile, what each tool is for and how it
 is started, and which well-known tools are not packaged and where their
 vendors publish them. Used by the Arsenal manager and by the
 nexus-arsenal-* metapackages.
 .
 This package contains manifests only: no tools, exploit code, payloads,
 word lists or credentials.

Package: nexus-arsenal-core
Architecture: all
Section: metapackages
Depends:
