 socat,
 sslscan,
 tcpdump,
 whatweb,
 whois,
 wireshark,
 zenmap
Suggests: nexus-arsenal
Description: NEXUS Arsenal profile - Core Security
 A compact, broadly useful set of command-line and graphical tools for
 authorized security work: host and service discovery, a packet analyser, TLS
 checks, a password manager and the common network utilities the other
 profiles build on. Like every profile it is installed on demand; start here,
 the specialised profiles add to it.
 .
 This metapackage recommends the 15 tools of the profile, all from Debian
 main; APT installs them with it. A tool can be removed again without removing
 the profile.
 .
 Not included, because they are not in Debian main: Metasploit Framework. The
 Arsenal manager lists where their vendors publish them.
 .
 These tools are for authorised security testing, research, defence and
 education only: use them on systems you own or have explicit written
 permission to test, and follow the law that applies to you. They come with no
 warranty.

